son</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><article-title>Past infection with hepatitis A virus among Vancouver street youth, injection drug users and men who have sex with men: Implications for vaccination programs</article-title><source>CMAJ</source><year>2001</year><volume>165</volume><fpage>293</fpage><lpage>297</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11517645</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B24"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Majumdar</surname><given-names>BB</given-names></name><name><surname>Chambers</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Roberts</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><article-title>Community-based, culturally sensitive HIV/AIDS education for Aboriginal adolescents: Implications for nursing practice</article-title><source>J Transcult Nurs</source><year>2004</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>73</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/1043659603260015</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14768418</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="B25"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><name><surname>Darke</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><article-title>Self-report among injecting drug users: A review</article-title><source>Drug Alcohol Depend</source><year>1998</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>263</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0376-8716(98)00028-3</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9787998</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>